# DTF tier manifest: project-admin-and-project-quota
#   (artifact-keeper#2473 and #2474 / #2475, all shipped in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. Everything under test is the management
# API and upload admission ahead of the storage backend; the oracle is HTTP
# plus direct reads of the DB.
#
# THE FEATURES
#   #2473  A principal holding `admin` in a project grant (the four actions
#          admin/read/write/delete through POST /projects/{id}/members) may
#          GET/PUT that project and list/add/remove its members, and may
#          POST /repositories when the request assigns the repository to that
#          project. Listing/creating/deleting projects, changing quota_bytes
#          and the global /permissions API stay global-admin-only; a token
#          restricted to a repository allowlist is never a project admin. A
#          repository created through project admin alone records created_by
#          but gets no repository-owner role, so removing the creator from the
#          project removes their access. A key that uses another project's
#          `<project.key>-` prefix is a 400, even for the global admin.
#          Reassigning a repository to another project needs project admin on
#          the destination; repository admin alone is a 403.
#   #2474  projects.quota_bytes was stored but ignored. Upload admission now
#          checks the project aggregate: 507 QUOTA_EXCEEDED "Project storage
#          quota exceeded".
#   #2475  npm publish skipped the quota check entirely; it is now admitted
#          against the repository and project quotas.
#
# ORACLE (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1)
#   (CONTROL) every image: the global admin manages projects and members; a
#     grant-less user and a project admin are both refused project list /
#     create, a quota change, the global /permissions API, a repository
#     outside the project; a repository-restricted token of the project admin
#     is refused the project; a repository key with the project's OWN prefix
#     and an unprefixed key are accepted; the repository admin can still PATCH
#     the description; uploads into a repository outside any project and an
#     npm publish into an npm repository outside any project succeed.
#   (FIX) RED on 1.10.0, GREEN on 1.11.0 and later: project admin GET/PUT,
#     member list/add/remove, repository create in the project without an
#     owner role, access ends when the membership is removed; another
#     project's key prefix 400; reassignment by a repository admin 403; the
#     second upload across two member repositories 507 with the project
#     message; npm publish over the project quota 507.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: four principals, ~70 back-to-back calls.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
